pouch boundary-line patch 0047 - file maps through SYS_BURROW_MAP_FILE (B-1d).

B-1d of the browser arc (ARCHITECTURE.md sec 6.5 "Dynamic loading";
docs/browser-status.md "The B-1 decisions", rows 5, 6 and 14). libc.so is
musl's own loader, and its map_library (ldso/dynlink.c) places an object
with three map shapes: the whole span at an address the kernel chooses
(:809), each later segment MAP_FIXED over it (:842), and the bss tail
anonymously (:848). Until this patch every file-backed mmap was ENOSYS. The
kernel serves the file shapes as SYS_BURROW_MAP_FILE (126), DISTRO D-3's
arms under their native name, with the vouching rule on every executable
window: a Dev that may back code, on a mount not marked MNOEXEC, else
EACCES (POSIX's answer; Linux's EPERM is the phenotype's). Two files:

  src/internal/_pouch_mman.h  SYS_thyla_burrow_map_file 126 and its one
      flag, POUCH_BURROW_MAP_FIXED (`addr` is read only under it).

  src/mman/mmap.c  A MAP_PRIVATE file map goes to 126. Without MAP_FIXED,
      the span is mapped read-only or executable where the kernel chooses.
      The address hint is dropped (the kernel refuses a nonzero one), so an
      ET_EXEC run through the loader fails its exact-address check with
      EBUSY and only a PIE or a .so loads -- the 2026-09-24 vote. With
      MAP_FIXED, the window at `start` is replaced: a read-only or
      executable window shares the file's pages through the Image cache,
      and a writable one is an eager private copy, charged now. The bss
      tail is not a file map: it is MAP_FIXED|MAP_ANON over the writable
      segment's copy, which is plain anonymous memory, so 0044's discard +
      reprotect serves it unchanged.
      Answered before the kernel: a negative fd is EBADF, because the
      kernel reads fd -1 under its FIXED flag as the anonymous window and a
      request without MAP_ANON must never become one. MAP_SHARED and
      MAP_SHARED_VALIDATE, a writable map without MAP_FIXED, a map without
      read, and MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE are ENOSYS, which is the domain the
      Linux phenotype's two file arms admit (kernel/vivarium.c), so the
      two substrates agree on what is served. len 0 (EINVAL) and len >=
      PTRDIFF_MAX (ENOMEM) are checked for both halves, before the split.

The witness is B-1d's dlopen probe on the device: a Pouch-built .so loaded
by a Pouch host, whose four -z separate-loadable-segments segments drive
every shape, and its MNOEXEC deny leg. The kernel half is the map_file.*
unit tests.

